<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marico River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marico River is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s North West province that flows north from the western highveld to join the Crocodile River, the two together forming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a>. The surrounding Marico district was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahurutshe">Bahurutshe</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana people</a>, and in 1837 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mzilikazi">Mzilikazi</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> there, after which the Ndebele moved north across the Limpopo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marico-river.jpg" alt="Marico River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guest9999 (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River,_Madikwe_Game_Reserve.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
